hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2709","\n Narrated to us Muhammad bin Bashshar, who said: Narrated to us Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, who said: Narrated to us Ja'far, who said: My father narrated to me, saying: We went to Jabir bin Abdullah and asked him about the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ). He said: \We set out intending only Hajj until we reached the Ka'bah. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) touched the Black Stone"","" then he performed Ramal (walking briskly with shoulders"""""
"2710","Narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la and 'Isa ibn Ibrahim. Yunus said: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Yunus informed me. 'Isa said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn 'Abdullah, from his father (Abdullah ibn 'Umar), who said:\n\I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) when he entered Makkah"","" he would touch the Black Stone (al-Rukn al-Aswad) as the first thing he did when starting the Tawaf. During the first three circuits of the seven"","" he would walk briskly (yakhbu).\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
